# Topic branches merged to build the integration branch, in order.
# Drop a line once upstream accepts that work; it then arrives via upstream/main.
# perf-skip-pod-list-deserialization was dropped this way when it merged as #201,
# then workload-indexing-and-node-naming (#218) and step-script-fixes (#217).
#
# Each branch stays whole rather than being split further: the upstream
# maintainer's cost is per-pull-request, not per line reviewed, so fewer and
# larger changesets move faster through their process.
#
# This branch is rebuilt onto newer upstream rather than accumulating commits, so
# its tip is not a stable reference. Builds pin an immutable build/<n> tag
# instead -- see the rundeck-k8s-plugin-build repository.
#
# Rebuild with:
#   git fetch upstream && git fetch origin
#   git show integration:INTEGRATION > /tmp/INTEGRATION
#   git checkout -B integration upstream/main
#   cp /tmp/INTEGRATION INTEGRATION && git add INTEGRATION \
#     && git commit -m 'Add INTEGRATION list of topic branches for the integration build'
#   grep -v '^#' INTEGRATION | while read -r b; do git merge --no-edit "$b" || break; done
build-config
quiet-container-status-logging
